{"title":"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute-angled triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/d/dcd9a79b499a99a34e164f71a92b0727f50109c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &lt; AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. The perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c83b9df54f6ae469b584cd80f26d39255ffc7041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43a2070858da2305a10781e5249b1ea7639a7e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E \\neq A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />. The line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meets line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Denote the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/74577a535149ffa62098ac21eed6bec76b5f8393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15c30f9fb9f513cc02b19541e52803ebfc829760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\neq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />. Prove that the line tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> meets line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c83b9df54f6ae469b584cd80f26d39255ffc7041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> on the internal angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JhThDz0H7cI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JhThDz0H7cI</a> [Video contains solutions to all day 1 problems]\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/I4FoXeVnSpM?si=BMxwsH4thsZ-7uLF\">https://youtu.be/I4FoXeVnSpM?si=BMxwsH4thsZ-7uLF</a>\n[Video contains IMO 2023 P2 motivation + discussion] (~little-fermat)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2023_IMO_2o.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/46/2023_IMO_2o.png/250px-2023_IMO_2o.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"228\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/46/2023_IMO_2o.png/375px-2023_IMO_2o.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/46/2023_IMO_2o.png/500px-2023_IMO_2o.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2023_IMO_2o0.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/aa/2023_IMO_2o0.png/400px-2023_IMO_2o0.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"306\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/aa/2023_IMO_2o0.png/600px-2023_IMO_2o0.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/aa/2023_IMO_2o0.png/800px-2023_IMO_2o0.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Denote the point diametrically opposite to a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef032244f01b7e92b57f825f25c1e88325c59c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39; \\implies AS&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> is the internal angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Denote the crosspoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c83b9df54f6ae469b584cd80f26d39255ffc7041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d55e373f747ff168c5e97b2b512af12d3e20b9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AS&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed513acdb58a8d0326e4ae49c5ed949c1ae3093f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H, \\angle ABS = \\varphi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3515ddb494aeeb34ba8ccec5a9f4be422a3516.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AE \\perp BC, SS&#39; \\perp BC \\implies \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {AS} = \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {ES&#39;} = 2\\varphi \\implies\\]\" width=\"385\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79cf39386876732b72dbec60a6d96bfe65463516.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle EAS&#39; = \\varphi = \\angle ABS \\implies \\angle DAH = \\angle ABH \\implies\\]\" width=\"400\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/23073bd0ad010beaea5bebe317ff4ee97f4ffb00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\triangle AHD \\sim \\triangle BAH \\implies \\frac {AH}{BH} = \\frac {DH}{AH} \\implies AH^2 = BH \\cdot DH.\\]\" width=\"482\" height=\"37\" />\nTo finishing the solution we need only to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/98443c69ac50e5b2b6db2edd589d2a63d5092b97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PH = AH.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d30c3b3007b025cbb180686099a3862b144edc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F = SS&#39; \\cap AC \\implies \\angle CBS = \\frac {\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {CS}}{2}  = \\frac {\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {BS}}{2}  =  \\frac {\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {AB}}{2} +  \\frac {\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {AS}}{2} =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"459\" height=\"49\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06617987b1e0fa330b30656cd84da3c670c5d910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\angle FCB + \\varphi \\implies \\angle FBS = \\angle ABS \\implies H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"358\" height=\"18\" /> is incenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e616dde1a27f0a8bc0f24590b60dca8052fdc20c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABF.$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c44d250528247baf92ac8bd2ca1f3ca93ffba1ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = S&#39;B \\cap SA \\implies SB \\perp TS&#39;, S&#39;A \\perp TS \\implies H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"402\" height=\"19\" /> is the orthocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b8825b31f53e7ec61fddcbb2a79b15d0f1b3c230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle TSS&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"19\" /> \n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c9fa67755ec037857b45d9f3756a55f60d01b7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G = PS&#39; \\cap AE \\implies \\angle BPG = \\angle BPS&#39; = \\angle BSS&#39; = \\angle BDG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"471\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/078595d557a982fb71ede9d3edc84949212d41aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies B, L, P, D,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are concyclic.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2023_IMO_2_lemma.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/2023_IMO_2_lemma.png/300px-2023_IMO_2_lemma.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"239\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/2023_IMO_2_lemma.png/450px-2023_IMO_2_lemma.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/2023_IMO_2_lemma.png/600px-2023_IMO_2_lemma.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure> \n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b57c0f5cd39648d7c1b5982069b26d8595b5494f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EBS&#39; = \\varphi, \\angle LBG = \\angle LDG = 90^\\circ = \\angle DBS&#39; \\implies \\angle DBG = \\varphi = \\angle SBF \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"638\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541a82cb53219d48299ec53bb5543cc20ebc8a59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B, G,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef2e20f46b4e612a3afb14197f2aa75599e01170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies GF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> is symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a494a942f1a33327f559aa3d3b017b2a44edcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We use the lemma and complete the proof.\n</p><p><i><b>Lemma 1</b></i>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2023_IMO_2b_Lemma.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/ec/2023_IMO_2b_Lemma.png/300px-2023_IMO_2b_Lemma.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"239\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/ec/2023_IMO_2b_Lemma.png/450px-2023_IMO_2b_Lemma.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/ec/2023_IMO_2b_Lemma.png/600px-2023_IMO_2b_Lemma.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/788dd157b230be6db8ae7846fb262afd34538956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, AB &gt; AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" /> be given.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the orthocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00d3cc85ab724d483b0f41d61a586e28dc752698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, BHD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> be the height.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> be the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c81603ee4f315f053ccca521e82353ede0a45ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD. BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" /> is the diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de82b5de37f029271b42d807a7a35ac5a7e8e7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64a6e1544c9db765796e7fe8df0748cbb1d701b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdb888672fd2539c7669d9698d18cbff8b1f24a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F \\neq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d34a68ae4a466f75013c7b1cc1a846e2cc626e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HF = HD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/c/21ceaedc991a3189e37d438c72776ef58dd09dbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/553218a29c6cfc03ebba72f8a1bd57a5ced301c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F&#39; \\neq D, HD = HF&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"19\" /> \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d07f3ec0b503bb2c17f14706a0badb819daed278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/7/b9770132f1ae529fef99311387752df12a1fe69d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39; \\neq F&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>We use Reim’s theorem for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee1dd9170f4dc324ad1f2c57f1bb478677d2b1fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega, \\Omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> and lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a7209ebfd255c60845d86a82372c2c5f7d13d0b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e43825ae1a9e5bbd76e1c39c9e56f05ec55b8bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE&#39;F&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/97851785d915b73d97b5a9ab6264ce1cbad584c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;D || BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>(this idea was recommended by <i><b>Leonid Shatunov</b></i>).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28ecc866d8ed594ad961f3a8d277c82890ee8cbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH \\perp BC \\implies AH \\perp E&#39;D \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"268\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411ef29ce6c32ab71534dfd3319a6fe72af9c5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc0ce4f028f277d0c677682c4c1d24cfd27e4edb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH \\implies E&#39; = E \\implies F&#39; = F \\implies HF = HD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"388\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. We proceed with showing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/c/6bc5f43d2cc43cb3341742aa1a739ec369c703e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PH=AH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d6394023b7f71962bce796b61343dcc276679c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5ec66f3f457c501d3289f7af41a1a834f681dce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SS&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e09ef0ed4e2a54517b0aa0c30005b9161299947d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F \\ne A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. Note that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e78a0b62fb3701aeb1393e6e5097a4884f78b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle CBE=\\angle DLE=\\angle DPB=\\angle FCB \\implies EF \\| BC.\\]\" width=\"416\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436b7897c320f3a214bbe61fe527488a79265ed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE \\perp BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/525faff7bc480b8ce292d7b847e7b3b55b860d44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE \\perp EF$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />. By similar triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47da4736612632542bb75a3c42440bab39a21aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ=\\frac{1}{2}AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" /> and therefore\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59bcbf3423bd918572b07ef666e2668e669ff29.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{SO}{OQ}=\\frac{SS&#39;}{AD}=\\frac{SH}{HD} \\implies OH \\| DQ.\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c311c04f367f20328b5eb8ffb00a6940095ffb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FP \\perp AP \\implies OH \\perp AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"215\" height=\"14\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. This proves the claim.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Identify <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> with the unit circle, and let the internal bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa0cf5ac208f05d89e99fb14e0a802452ceac9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{BS}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"21\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. We set up so that\n\\begin{align*}\n|a|=|b|=|s|&amp;=1 \\\\\nc &amp;= \\frac{s^2}b \\\\\nt &amp;= -s \\\\\ne = -\\frac{bc}a &amp;= -\\frac{s^2}a \\\\\nd = \\frac{ae(b+s) - bs(a+e)}{ae-bs} &amp;= \\frac{a^2b+abs+as^2-bs^2}{a(b+s)} \\\\\nq = \\frac{at(b+s) - bs(a+t)}{at-bs} &amp;= \\frac{2ab+as-bs}{a+b}\n\\end{align*}\nNow we find the coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/8584548ddcebdd57a179a100f85f5f694312a773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|p|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04b69bc0abd3d262eee825a3965bbf7d23707d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(b-p)(d-\\ell)}{(b-\\ell)(d-p)} \\in \\mathbb{R}\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"43\" />\nNow <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a8d802333dc4b5411a30d5bd15c812ca802be42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d-\\ell}{b-c}, \\frac{b-\\ell}{b-e} \\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"131\" height=\"41\" />. Thus we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80cd7788f428c3d3c0877359f156eaccfd1a0a6f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(b-p)(b-c)}{(b-e)(d-p)} \\in \\mathbb{R}\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"43\" />\nand so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d51d3bbfa59b38351f687dc947154bd9c082e7b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^2(b-p)(b+s)^2(b-s)}{b(ab+s^2)(a^2b+abs+as^2-bs^2-abp-aps)} = \\frac{as(b-p)(b+s)^2(b-s)}{b(ab+s^2)(ps^2+aps+abp-a^2p-as^2-abs)}\\]\" width=\"744\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04222ce7e281f5d96c3830426f29a08b2599e4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a(ps^2+aps+abp-a^2p-as^2-abs) = s(a^2b+abs+as^2-bs^2-abp-aps)\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0ea45ff3ed0ac57454a90b23999aae3d44a4207.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2aps^2+a^2ps+a^2bp-a^3p-a^2s^2-2a^2bs-abs^2-as^3+bs^3+abps = 0\\]\" width=\"539\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4ddd25009445eca9451119137efc12cc9156cb8d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p = \\frac{2a^2bs+abs^2+as^3+a^2s^2-bs^3}{2as^2+a^2s+a^2b+abs-a^3} = \\frac{s(2ab+as-bs)}{a(2s+b-a)}\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"44\" />\nIt remains to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> lies on the tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Define the vectors\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b1695ea241c01d63733013a8ab485bcb873a3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b&#39; = b-p = \\frac{(b-a)(ab+s^2)}{a(2s+b-a)}\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"44\" />\nand\n\\begin{align*}\nd' = d-p &amp;= \\frac{(2s+b-a)(a^2b+abs+as^2-bs^2) - s(b+s)(2ab+as-bs)}{a(b+s)(2s+b-a)} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{a^2bs+as^3-bs^3+a^2b^2-a^3b-a^2s^2+abs^2-ab^2s}{a(b+s)(2s+b-a)} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{(a-s)(b-a)(ab+s^2)}{a(b+s)(2s+b-a)}\n\\end{align*}\nWe observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10e726ddd616756eda2bc33c439f6d8b7f2252a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{b&#39;} = -\\frac{b&#39;}{bp}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"74\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bfcbe36faf28a199564766868e3b070115659e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{d&#39;} = \\frac{d&#39;}{ap}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"63\" height=\"43\" />. Thus if we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c89e23e0d2b9340308f19426f7a3ba50352e851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o&#39; = o-p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b500641ac3ba32c3df32ba6a4788b5a742334596.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[o&#39; = \\frac{b&#39;d&#39;(\\overline{b&#39;}-\\overline{d&#39;})}{\\overline{b&#39;}d&#39;-b&#39;\\overline{d&#39;}} = \\frac{ab&#39;+bd&#39;}{a+b} = \\frac{\\frac{(b-a)(ab+s^2)}{2s+b-a} + \\frac{b(a-s)(b-a)(ab+s^2)}{a(b+s)(2s+b-a)}}{a+b} = \\frac{(b-a)(ab+s^2)(2ab+as-bs)}{a(a+b)(b+s)(2s+b-a)}\\]\" width=\"753\" height=\"52\" />\nMeanwhile, we compute\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d62623cd8d81fdded254197175cfc4d056f42cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[q-p = \\frac{2ab+as-bs}{a+b} - \\frac{s(2ab+as-bs)}{a(2s+b-a)} = \\frac{(a-s)(b-a)(2ab+as-bs)}{a(a+b)(2s+b-a)}\\]\" width=\"565\" height=\"43\" />\nSo\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d0cd7f47322055fe08f18066184c255cc4ee5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{o-p}{q-p} = \\frac{(ab+s^2)}{(a-s)(b+s)}\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"44\" />\nwhich is pure imaginary. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n~approved by Kislay kai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO\" title=\"2023 IMO\">2023 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017030250\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.059 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 693/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 24047/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.927      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.927      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24783:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017030250 and revision id 225592. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}